  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 207 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nUpper level ridging remains in control of our weather pattern \nthrough much of the forecast period. The center of the ridge \ngradually shifts from the southern Plains into the Desert Southwest \nthrough the remainder of the week and much of the weekend. \nSubsidence below this area of high pressure keeps hot and mostly dry \nconditions in the forecast. Temperatures most afternoons are progged \nto range within the 90s to low 100s. The hottest conditions are \nforecast to arise on Friday afternoon, when highs beyond the triple \ndigit mark become more prevalent, especially within the Big Country.\nAs such, heat products may be issued as needed later this week. However,\nmodels indicate a slight cool down late this weekend. As the ridge\ncontinues a westward shift Saturday, a trough currently over the eastern\nUS looks to dip southward, sending a cold front into the region Saturday\nafternoon. The front brings slightly cooler temperatures Sunday and\nMonday. Lift associated with the front also brings low (<20%) rain chances\nto the region Saturday and Sunday afternoons. Otherwise, overnight lows\nare forecast to generally settle into the 70s each night.",
